# Claude Code session state. `launch.json` is tracked shared dev config; the rest
# is per-session scratch, and `worktrees/` would nest a second copy of the repo.
.claude/*
!.claude/launch.json

# Checkpoints and deliverables of `scripts/seed_concepts.py` -- all regenerable.
# Anchored to the repo root, and the slash at the front is load-bearing: the
# unanchored `learning/` matched ANY directory of that name at any depth, which
# includes `backend/app/learning/` and `backend/tests/learning/`. Files already
# tracked there survived, but every NEW file was silently swallowed -- a test
# written for app/learning/health.py sat on disk, ran green locally, and never
# entered a commit. `git add -A` reported nothing, because ignored is not the
# same as unstaged.
/learning/
